{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"99f730b5-8ed4-49a9-9e78-c6e7661c8649","outcome":{"verdict":"approved","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/single-phase-archive/review-feedback-003.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"tests/unit/core/archive/orchestrator.test.ts","title":"TC-022: headSha acquisition not asserted after push-skip path","rationale":"TC-022 (must-priority) in test-cases.md specifies: 'headSha は従来どおり git rev-parse HEAD で取得される'. The test verifies exitCode 0 and absence of push, but does not assert that `git rev-parse HEAD` was spawned, nor that `result.headSha` is defined. The implementation at orchestrator.ts L354 correctly calls rev-parse before the early return, but the assertion is missing. T-02 AC also lists this as a required behaviour.","line":894},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/archive/plain-archive.ts","title":"Path B omits explicit finishable gate; comment should document why","rationale":"design.md D5 Path B states execution order: 'finishable gate → markJobArchived(slug, cwd) → cleanup'. Path A enforces this via assertJobFinishable inside the orchestrator (Phase 0). Path B bypasses assertJobFinishable entirely, relying on the transitionJob internal validation inside markJobArchived to throw (which is then caught and treated as a warning). The behaviour is functionally safe and consistent with the best-effort semantics ('transition 失敗は warning に留め cleanup を続行'), but the omission is inconsistent with the design doc wording. A comment explaining the intentional omission is the minimum required fix.","line":127}],"evidence":{"checked":43,"skipped":1,"unverified":1},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/archive/__tests__/plain-archive.test.ts","title":"TC-043 (must) is transitively but not directly verified","rationale":"TC-043 ('--from-issue invocation completes in one run', must-priority) is covered transitively: the CLI test shows runPlainArchive is called, and TC-001 proves runPlainArchive completes in one run. There is no direct end-to-end test for the --from-issue resolve chain. Acceptable given the structural decomposition but worth noting for future follow-up.","line":23},{"severity":"low","file":"specrunner/adr/2026-08-21-archive-state-after-merge.md","title":"Superseded ADR link points to spec.md; adr-gen will create the actual ADR","rationale":"The old ADR's 'superseded by' link currently targets ../changes/single-phase-archive/spec.md. The actual new ADR (with Amends: header) will be generated by adr-gen at step 12. T-09-pre checkboxes in tasks.md are intent markers for adr-gen, not completed work items. No action required at code-review stage.","line":5}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-27T04:46:07.395Z","endedAt":"2026-08-27T04:57:21.266Z","commitOid":"aaeb27ba5f0c2cff16ccd30db657c8be8ddc4a4a"}
